Since you already have Minikube, kubectl, and Helm on your Ubuntu VM, follow these steps to install and configure ArgoCD.

1. Create ArgoCD Namespace
Shell
kubectl create namespace argocd

Verify:

Shell
kubectl get ns
 
2. Install ArgoCD

Apply the official manifest:

Shell
kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml

Check pods:

Shell
kubectl get pods -n argocd

Expected pods:

Shell
argocd-server
argocd-application-controller
argocd-repo-server
argocd-dex-server
argocd-redis

Wait until all pods are:

Shell
Running
3. Check ArgoCD Services
Shell
kubectl get svc -n argocd

You should see:

Shell
argocd-server
argocd-repo-server
argocd-metrics
 
4. Expose ArgoCD UI
Option 1: Port Forward (Recommended for Minikube)

Open a new terminal:

Shell
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443
 

Open browser:

Plain Text
https://localhost:8080

Accept the SSL warning.

Option 2: NodePort

Patch service:

Shell
kubectl patch svc argocd-server -n argocd \
-p '{"spec":{"type":"NodePort"}}'
 

Check port:

Shell
kubectl get svc argocd-server -n argocd

Example:

Shell
NAME TYPE PORT(S)
argocd-server NodePort 80:32080/TCP

Get Minikube IP:

Shell
minikube ip
 

Open:

Plain Text
http://<MINIKUBE-IP>:32080
5. Get Initial Admin Password

Username:

Plain Text
admin

Password:

Shell
kubectl -n argocd \
get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret \
-o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d

Example output:

Shell
mY7kLpXxA2

Login with:

Plain Text
Username : admin
Password : mY7kLpXxA2
6. Install ArgoCD CLI

Download:

Shell
curl -sSL -o argocd \
https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd/releases/latest/download/argocd-linux-amd64

Make executable:

Shell
chmod +x argocd
sudo mv argocd /usr/local/bin/

Verify:

Shell
argocd version
7. Login Using CLI
Shell
argocd login localhost:8080 \
--username admin \
--password <password> \
--insecure

Check:

Shell
argocd cluster list
8. Add GitHub Repository

Example:

Shell
argocd repo add \
https://github.com/yourname/gitops-demo.git
 

Verify:

Shell
argocd repo list
9. Create First Application

Suppose GitHub contains:

Plain Text
k8s/
├── deployment.yaml
└── service.yaml

Create application:

Shell
argocd app create nginx-app \
--repo https://github.com/yourname/gitops-demo.git \
--path k8s \
--dest-server https://kubernetes.default.svc \
--dest-namespace default

Sync:

Shell
argocd app sync nginx-app

Check:

Shell
argocd app get nginx-app
10. Auto Sync Configuration

Enable GitOps auto-deployment:

Shell
argocd app set nginx-app \
--sync-policy automated

Now whenever code changes in GitHub:

Plain Text
GitHub Commit
↓
ArgoCD Detects Change
↓
Syncs Kubernetes
↓
Pods Updated
